WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 7: Nature’s Power.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.420
Welcome to Unit 7: Nature’s Power!

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:14.400
In this unit, you will explore the incredible and
sometimes dangerous forces of the natural world.

4
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:21.000
You will learn about natural disasters such as cyclones,
earthquakes, floods, droughts, and volcanic eruptions.

5
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:27.120
You will discover how communities in East Africa
and around the world prepare for these events,

6
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.780
respond when they strike, and rebuild afterwards.

7
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.880
Along the way, you will build a strong set of vocabulary
words related to planning, science, government,

8
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.120
and community action.

9
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:46.400
You will also study an important grammar topic — how to
use the Past Simple and Past Continuous tenses together,

10
00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:53.720
joined by connecting words like while, when, and until — to
describe events that happened at the same time in the past.

11
00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:54.910
These...

12
00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.680
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:09.520
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use and understand
key vocabulary about natural forces, science, planning,

14
00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.060
government, and community.

15
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:17.300
you will also read and discuss a text about natural
disasters and how communities respond to them.

16
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:25.960
you will also identify the past simple tense (for completed
actions) and the past continuous tense (for actions that

17
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.680
were happening when something else occurred).

18
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.060
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

19
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:39.500
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: conduction,
pollination, stratosphere, excavation, mechanization,

20
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:40.300
illustration.

21
00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:46.340
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

22
00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.880
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

23
00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:56.870
The reading sequence includes Nature’s Power:
source text 1 and Nature’s Power: source text 2.

24
00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.260
Read actively.

25
00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.660
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

26
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.640
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

27
00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:11.380
The first language focus is Past Simple vs Past Continuous.

28
00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:17.440
What it means and why it matters The Past
Simple describes actions that are finished.

29
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:24.360
The Past Continuous describes actions that were happening
— still in progress — at a certain moment in the past.

30
00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.100
When we use them together,

31
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.280
we can tell vivid stories about events that
happened at the same time or interrupted each other.

32
00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.780
This is especially useful when
describing natural disasters, emergencies,

33
00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.780
or any event where many things were happening at once.

34
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.340
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

35
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:51.080
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

36
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.680
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

37
00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.180
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

38
00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.440
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

39
00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:03.820
You are ready to begin.

40
00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:10.120
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

41
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.900
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

42
00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:18.880
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
